            <ArticleTitle>Epidural analgesia associated with a fatal outcome in a patient with an unrecognized brain tumour.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>832-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fatality associated with epidural analgesia in a patient with an unsuspected brain tumour has not been reported in the literature. We describe a case of postoperative lumbar epidural analgesia in a 54-year-old female patient who had an undiagnosed brain tumour and a fatal outcome postoperatively. The factors that potentially contributed to this mishap and the possible alternative management of this patient are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
